# Line endings.
#
# Text files are stored with LF in the repository whatever the platform of the
# author, and git converts them to the native ending on checkout
# (core.autocrlf). Before this file existed the index held a mix of CRLF and LF
# blobs, so editing a file on Windows produced a diff that rewrote every line of
# it and made the real change impossible to review.
* text=auto

# Scripts that only ever run on Windows keep CRLF, so that cmd.exe and
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 are happy even in a checkout with autocrlf=false.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
